    <string name="section_faq">Quick Help &amp; OEM Guides</string>
    <string name="faq_how_it_works_title">How WhiteCall Works</string>
    <string name="faq_how_it_works_desc">WhiteCall uses Android\'s CallScreeningService to inspect incoming calls in real-time. If the caller is not in your White List (or contacts if enabled), the call is instantly rejected with zero ringtone or vibration.</string>
    <string name="faq_permissions_title">Required Permissions</string>
    <string name="faq_permissions_desc">• Call Screening Role: To block calls silently.\n• Contacts: To let your saved contacts reach you.\n• Phone State: To read caller metadata.</string>
    <string name="faq_oem_title">Xiaomi / Samsung / Huawei Background Settings</string>
    <string name="faq_oem_desc">To prevent the system from killing WhiteCall:\n• Xiaomi (MIUI/HyperOS): Enable Autostart in App Info, set Battery Saver to "No restrictions".\n• Samsung: Add WhiteCall to "Never sleeping apps" under Battery Settings.\n• Huawei: Set Launch settings to "Manage manually" and allow background activity.</string>

